  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Korba?", answer: "Tell us the programme, subject, level and exam session, and we shortlist tutors who have genuinely taught that course. With no IB school anywhere in the district, matching runs on syllabus fit rather than location, and we then settle on a lesson time your evening can actually hold. A free trial lesson comes before any decision, and we find someone else if the first match does not work." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE home tutors in Korba for Cambridge and Edexcel?", answer: "Both boards, yes, delivered as online home tuition rather than a house visit. Cambridge students are matched by syllabus code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 as examples, and Edexcel students by specification and Foundation or Higher tier, always working from each board's own past papers and mark schemes." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Korba?", answer: "They do not. Home visits are limited to Gurugram and a handful of Delhi NCR neighbourhoods; a Korba lesson runs live online instead, one to one over video, with a shared whiteboard standing in for whatever a physical visit would otherwise cover. Call it private tuition at home minus the doorbell." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor cost in Korba?", answer: "It depends on the programme and level, the subject, session length and how recently the tutor has taught it, and that figure is confirmed for your specific match before the trial lesson. IB Diploma HL subjects generally run higher than MYP or IGCSE Core. Every session is online, so no travel charge gets folded in, and nothing here commits you to a long contract." },
    { question: "Does any school in Korba actually teach IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not as far as schoolmykids.com shows; no school in the district appears against either the IB or Cambridge/Edexcel IGCSE. Local schooling runs through CGBSE, CBSE and PSU-linked campuses tied to NTPC, SECL and BALCO, DAV Public School in Kusmunda among them. A Korba family after these curricula is almost always working through an online school or a distance provider, which is why our tutoring stays entirely online." },
    { question: "If not locally, where do Korba families look for an IB school?", answer: "Some stay in Korba and enrol through an online IB or IGCSE provider, leaning on tutoring to cover whatever that provider leaves thin. Others, especially ahead of secondary school, look toward Raipur, about 200 kilometres away, where Rungta International School runs the state's first authorised IB programme." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial lesson before I commit to anything?", answer: "Always. Your child works through a genuine topic from their own syllabus with the tutor online, no charge and nothing owed afterwards. The tutor then puts together a short first-month plan, and from there you decide whether to continue, adjust the plan, or try a different tutor altogether." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments in Korba?", answer: "Guidance only, never the writing itself. That means shaping a workable research question, unpacking what an assessment criterion is actually rewarding, planning how data gets collected, and giving honest feedback on drafts. Writing or rewriting graded work breaches IB academic integrity rules, so it is always declined." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you cover for a Korba student?", answer: "All the major subject groups, with the most requested from families connected to Korba being Maths Analysis and Approaches or Applications and Interpretation at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, plus Theory of Knowledge and the Extended Essay." },
    { question: "Can you tutor IB MYP and PYP students connected to Korba, not just the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, across the entire continuum. MYP work generally centres on criterion-based analysis in the sciences and Language and Literature, plus the Personal Project journal, while PYP support covers reading, writing, number sense and Exhibition research, usually in short, regular sessions suited to a younger child." },
    { question: "Does online tutoring actually work as well as in-person help for IB or IGCSE in Korba?", answer: "It holds up well, especially given how few local specialists exist here for HL subjects or specific IGCSE codes. A shared whiteboard, screen-shared past papers and recorded worked solutions cover nearly everything a tutor sitting beside your child would otherwise do, while opening access to specialists across India rather than the handful in one district." },
    { question: "How does IB Gram actually check its tutors for Korba students?", answer: "Qualifications, how recently a tutor has taught that exact subject and level, and how they approach assessment criteria, all get checked before any introduction. Given how thin Korba's pool genuinely is, we specifically look for someone who has taught the syllabus recently rather than a generalist, and the free trial lesson lets you judge the rest yourself." },
    { question: "When is the right time for a Korba student to start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Right at the start of the course ideally, Class 11 for the Diploma and Grade 9 for IGCSE, leaving time to shore up foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades arrive. Starting later, even in the final year, can still help if the plan sticks to the highest-value topics and past papers." },
    { question: "My child is moving from CGBSE or CBSE to IB or IGCSE. Can a tutor help with that switch?", answer: "This comes up fairly often from Korba, given how little runs IB or IGCSE locally from the start. The real gap is usually question style rather than content: command words like 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need direct teaching, along with new IA or coursework planning habits, ideally begun the summer before the switch." },
    { question: "Can sessions be scheduled on weekends or after school in Korba?", answer: "Yes, most families here book weekday evenings after school or weekend mornings. We work around the district's peak heat in April and May, when an earlier evening slot tends to suit better, and around Hareli and Pola. Adding a second weekly slot before mocks or an exam series is straightforward since everything already runs online." },
    { question: "What if the tutor is not the right fit for my child in Korba?", answer: "Say so and we will match someone else. We check in with families every few weeks and re-match whenever the fit is genuinely wrong, rather than expecting a child to push through with the wrong person. There is no long contract in the way, so pausing or stopping carries no penalty either." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any Korba school, NTPC, SECL, BALCO, or to the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No, on every count. IB Gram runs independently and has no affiliation with, endorsement from, or representation of any school, NTPC, South Eastern Coalfields, BALCO, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Everything named here simply describes the real curriculum landscape a Korba family is navigating, and tutors follow whatever calendar and syllabus each provider actually publishes." },
  ],

